        "location": "longterm-mem/cmd/longterm-mem/lineage.go:14-22",
        "claim": "Lineage is asymmetric. A memorycard memory mirrored by hand names its Engram twin observations, but the Engram observation's lineage only follows import_map rows. For hand-mirrored content, the observation gets no lineage, and the lineage test pins this. S3 bridges a memory when a page carries one of its lineage identities. Once T3 wires this in, an Engram walk would not recognise a page owned by the hand-mirrored memorycard memory and could promote the same content twice.",
